<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Denmark: Top court backs hardline immigration "ghetto law"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ddceb3e1959353dd6069318ae3f6b9005220e976dc7ea6f7b0d026c1b25fde1</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T20:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/denmark-top-court-backs-hardline-immigration-ghetto-law/a-80026478--7ebce97025f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/denmark-top-court-backs-hardline-immigration-ghetto-law/a-80026478?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denmark's Supreme Court has found that evictions of "non-Western" residents do not amount to discrimination. The government in Copenhagen argues its "ghetto law" encourages integration.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tajikistan follows US call, withdraws from ICC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b16abc08a32b9557e34eaf5a36a564077f4fb8290b3f21c7aaff62fba8580175</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tajikistan-follows-us-call-withdraws-from-icc/a-80023903--9937f6abaec0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tajikistan-follows-us-call-withdraws-from-icc/a-80023903?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tajikistan has initiated its withdrawal from the International Criminal Court as the US calls for it to be "dismantled." The decision was made during a recent visit from Russian President Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US and UK to host Women's World Cups in 2031 and 2035</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24fd8dc026bf9ca668e8171376e68e3abc26b7ba201f628c938ad5108fbaba2b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786--81630f151694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">FIFA has confirmed the United States, Mexico, Costa Rica and Jamaica will host the 2031 Women's World Cup — the first to feature 48 teams. The UK will stage the 2035 edition, its first World Cup since 1966.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Authorities search for lioness on the loose in Istanbul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e380209cb8ee4d7b1482bb4897b8b96f6a332673fef23839798ae70ca838a4d3</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-authorities-search-for-lioness-on-the-loose-in-istanbul/a-80020913--18544b4b5e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-authorities-search-for-lioness-on-the-loose-in-istanbul/a-80020913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A lioness was on the loose in northern Istanbul, with wildlife advocates demanding answers over how the animal entered the country and who was keeping it in captivity.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After Japan's APEC snub, what's next for its China ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:071e5f162e49634acf6f2a596f76e598003e1387ffac2147df10cb45545e60d2</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823--0940c063c8fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan has long-running concerns over Chinese military expansionism, and Beijing has bristled at Sanae Takaichi's comments on Taiwan. The frosty ties were on full display at the APEC summit.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7392fd1ad1eac7d30f29bf463780cc87fa1610860fe868c3a8ee95be0c72da13</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal's new PM eyes closer ties with India amid lingering disputes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd6836fd6dcde7f2974dd509dacff384b30c6aee49ea5196ed0f1b101380ac53</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769--65c0c20879de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On his first foreign bilateral visit, rapper-turned-Prime Minister Balendra Shah sought deeper ties with Nepal's neighbor and largest trading partner, while steering clear of sticky territorial issues.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a551c8c8477ff98c14ee3cf2dc5562ca1a8878a71341c32bfc859773b02af718</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926--88659c21678b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board voted unanimously to bring back the disgraced CEO, who resigned this month amid news of his affairs. He's suspected of having had a relationship with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Macedonia remains stalled on its EU path after 21 years as a candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb6b36986cad1fa3e30568d42d4540f6ecf40124d57f6373ac99def4653f410a</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841--291e539f1390.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU enlargement has regained momentum, with Montenegro and Albania moving closer to membership. But North Macedonia, a candidate since 2005, remains stalled by a politically difficult dispute involving Bulgaria.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda minister at COP31: 'We need a just transition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb9993c034e44e712c6129dd6d867941f2b157aac989b0904efd5ca64c474ad4</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:21:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209--312e033bb073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP deadlock prompts calls for a reset of climate diplomacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55a258e133aa731bbc9f8d9e4c339a22b21830adfb2cbe691c4e35cf20bd5d28</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494--3b4f8cad49dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">COP31 has been branded a failure after countries couldn't reach a final agreement, divided over a reference to "fossil fuels." But was the decision to walk away from a watered-down text actually a show of strength?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>German police respond to multiple school bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3b5fa0839157c494c551ccaff0f770cad261b7220bac349a69bc776a2724fda</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842--56ba1301d92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in Germany are responding to bomb threats against a series of schools, but say that at present they don't believe them to be credible. Danish authorities are reporting a similar series of apparent hoaxes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0888edfbafd929d280c31c81bc838e55d400c275e4309b8a30dd47f8d961c710</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Budget cuts threaten Germany's fight against antisemitism and racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ee670fe47048d3b05309084130b44520efcf240b68b56bb6155c58c78f7a1c3</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644--fcf379d5b1d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Numerous grassroots initiatives in Germany are facing funding cuts. Affected organizations are sounding the alarm, pointing to growing challenges posed by far-right extremism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Rembrandt's 'The Night Watch' is more alive than you'd expect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:496f7c08aef20c9295db14d8f3d0ea44e7baf23b05e5da9166a8b3e36aba00ee</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rembrandt-s-the-night-watch-is-more-alive-than-you-d-expect/a-79972540--0d1ff511f0b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rembrandt-s-the-night-watch-is-more-alive-than-you-d-expect/a-79972540?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new project and exhibition, "The Night Watch Lives," lifts the veil on the hidden world of microbes covering one of the most famous paintings of the Dutch Golden Age.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Early Start Pension: Can child investment accounts help?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:898e940c4ed3e8ab03d4bea2c6c0e8500d230584739041c9c34686bd934e23a0</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185--25ffc2424261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany plans to pay €10 a month into investment accounts for children to encourage long-term retirement saving. Economists say the measure may help build wealth but won't solve the country's pension funding challenge.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>NATO Parliamentary Assembly convenes amid Russian airspace violations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:819bf5f082a7f13ef0ad9f13ac3e8ff7905d7de7c9a464073d89599f5465663d</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nato-parliamentary-assembly-convenes-amid-russian-airspace-violations/live-80016415--9a53102043ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nato-parliamentary-assembly-convenes-amid-russian-airspace-violations/live-80016415?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy and German Foreign Minister Wadephul are set to address the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin while NATO representatives discuss Russian airspace violations in Brussels. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Kyiv claims strike that sank Russian ship off Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac74b592a8e7152ad9c849bcffaa6f2a004a5717ae627d98e2691676564b10b1</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-kyiv-claims-strike-that-sank-russian-ship-off-libya/live-80015859--bfcd59f235fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-kyiv-claims-strike-that-sank-russian-ship-off-libya/live-80015859?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said the attack was carried out with Ukrainian-made naval drones. Meanwhile, NATO members are meeting to discuss an alleged Russian violation of Polish airspace. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Metalworkers go on strike as pay dispute heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f492157beced87cdb13b46018552580b2a45fdb0cea6a25785421cc29f51ebb</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:21:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633--a1790c046188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest union is calling for more strikes over heated pay disputes with car makers like Mercedes and shipyards among the companies impacted. Meanwhile, a Berlin hospital fire leaves many injured. Follow DW.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Rule-breaking is contagious — and good examples barely help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0078c1d9efa5c276119d5d92d3e39b22263e7f3f399bfbc647fa5627412d92bc</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rule-breaking-is-contagious-and-good-examples-barely-help/a-79980025--098488c374ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rule-breaking-is-contagious-and-good-examples-barely-help/a-79980025?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seeing someone break a rule makes people more likely to break it too, a new study finds, especially when the rule-breaker is on their side politically. Watching others behave well barely made a difference.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Thousands protest closure of critical media outlets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95526ec9abb8ae3a3e8a52732c3fbbcc30f9fc805e37e5e8b5c90da09198fb1b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:21:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T21:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347--7bbb07b22139.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protesters gathered in Istanbul to show their support for press freedom in Turkey. The protest was called just days after the police raided Sozcu TV and arrested several senior staff members.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
